※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4498

※ The values fill the new object, going round again where there are fewer of
※ them than it holds.  More of them than it holds is the other way round and
※ has no reading: which ones would be left out is not something to guess at.

let v: u8⟦4⟧ = ⟦1u8, 2u8, 3u8, 4u8⟧

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let made: u8⟦2⟧ = 2 ⍴ v
    made⟦0⟧
